<section class="sp-hero"><div class="sp-hero-g"><div class="sp-hero-t"><p class="sp-k">&#9733; Slow food for busy weeknights &#9733;</p><h1>One pot. Low heat. Big flavour.</h1><p class="sp-lead">Stewpot is an independent home-cooking guide to stews, braises and one-pot dinners. Build a stew from what is in the cupboard, learn the simmer that keeps meat tender and plan a batch for the freezer.</p><a class="sp-btn" href="#builder">Build a stew tonight</a></div><figure class="sp-hero-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1764314108477-f026172e32a9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=760&h=760&q=75" alt="a hearty stew with chunks of meat and red chillies" width="760" height="760" fetchpriority="high"><div class="sp-steam" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></figure></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-lined" id="builder"><div class="sp-w"><div class="sp-sec-h"><p class="sp-k">The stew builder</p><h2>Four choices, one supper</h2><p class="sp-lead">Pick a base, a liquid, a flavour and how you will cook it. We will write the method and the times.</p></div><div class="sp-bld"><div class="sp-bld-f"><fieldset class="sp-step"><legend><span>1</span> Base of the stew</legend><div class="sp-opts"><label><input type="radio" name="base" value="0" checked><span>Beef chuck</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="base" value="1"><span>Chicken thighs</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="base" value="2"><span>Lamb shoulder</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="base" value="3"><span>Beans &amp; lentils</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="base" value="4"><span>Root vegetables</span></label></div></fieldset><fieldset class="sp-step"><legend><span>2</span> Liquid</legend><div class="sp-opts"><label><input type="radio" name="liquid" value="0" checked><span>Stock</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="liquid" value="1"><span>Chopped tomatoes</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="liquid" value="2"><span>Coconut milk</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="liquid" value="3"><span>Water + aromatics</span></label></div></fieldset><fieldset class="sp-step"><legend><span>3</span> Flavour</legend><div class="sp-opts"><label><input type="radio" name="flavour" value="0" checked><span>Smoky paprika</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="flavour" value="1"><span>Garden herbs</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="flavour" value="2"><span>Warm spices</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="flavour" value="3"><span>Chilli heat</span></label></div></fieldset><fieldset class="sp-step"><legend><span>4</span> Method</legend><div class="sp-opts"><label><input type="radio" name="method" value="0" checked><span>Stovetop</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="method" value="1"><span>Oven</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="method" value="2"><span>Slow cooker</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="method" value="3"><span>Pressure cooker</span></label></div></fieldset></div><div class="sp-card" id="bd-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-dark"><div class="sp-w sp-sim"><div><p class="sp-k">The golden rule</p><h2>Simmer, don&rsquo;t boil</h2><p class="sp-lead">A hard boil toughens meat and breaks vegetables apart. A lazy simmer, a bubble or two breaking the surface, turns tough cuts tender.</p><figure class="sp-sim-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793294329503-28676205cc37?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=340&q=75" alt="a lidded enamel pot on a stove in black and white" width="520" height="340" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="sp-bub"><div class="sp-bb sp-boil"><div class="sp-pot"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><b>Rolling boil</b><span>Big, fast bubbles. For pasta, never for stew.</span><em>&times; Too hot</em></div><div class="sp-bb sp-simr"><div class="sp-pot"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><b>Gentle simmer</b><span>Steady small bubbles. Good for beans and lentils.</span><em>&#10003; Fine</em></div><div class="sp-bb sp-lazy"><div class="sp-pot"><i></i><i></i></div><b>Lazy simmer</b><span>A bubble every second or two. Perfect for meat.</span><em>&#9733; Best</em></div></div></div></section>

<section class="sp-s"><div class="sp-w"><div class="sp-sec-h"><p class="sp-k">Postcards from the pot</p><h2>Stews around the world</h2><p class="sp-lead">Almost every kitchen has a slow-cooked one-pot dish. A few favourites:</p></div><ul class="sp-stamps"><li class="sp-stamp" style="--c:#B23A1E"><b>Chili</b><span>Southwest US</span><em>Beef or beans, chillies, cumin, tomato</em></li><li class="sp-stamp" style="--c:#7A3B1C"><b>Goulash</b><span>Hungary</span><em>Beef, onions, sweet paprika</em></li><li class="sp-stamp" style="--c:#C9772B"><b>Tagine</b><span>Morocco</span><em>Lamb or chicken, apricots, warm spices</em></li><li class="sp-stamp" style="--c:#E0A526"><b>Dal</b><span>India</span><em>Lentils, turmeric, cumin, ginger</em></li><li class="sp-stamp" style="--c:#5B4A2E"><b>Gumbo</b><span>Louisiana</span><em>Dark roux, okra, sausage, seafood</em></li><li class="sp-stamp" style="--c:#6E7F58"><b>Irish stew</b><span>Ireland</span><em>Lamb, potatoes, onions, thyme</em></li><li class="sp-stamp" style="--c:#2B1A12"><b>Feijoada</b><span>Brazil</span><em>Black beans, pork, orange slices</em></li><li class="sp-stamp" style="--c:#A04A2A"><b>Pot-au-feu</b><span>France</span><em>Beef, leeks, carrots, clear broth</em></li></ul></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-lined"><div class="sp-w sp-thk"><div><p class="sp-k">Too thin?</p><h2>Five ways to thicken a stew</h2><figure class="sp-thk-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1783335543126-9afdfff4d4ca?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=420&q=75" alt="cast iron pots cooking over a campfire" width="520" height="420" loading="lazy"></figure></div><ol class="sp-thk-l"><li><b>Reduce it</b><span>Simmer with the lid off for the last 20&ndash;30 minutes. Concentrates flavour too.</span><i style="--s:2">Speed</i></li><li><b>Flour the meat</b><span>Toss meat in a little flour before browning. Thickens as it cooks.</span><i style="--s:3">Speed</i></li><li><b>Cornflour slurry</b><span>Mix 1 tbsp with 2 tbsp cold water, stir in, simmer 2 minutes.</span><i style="--s:5">Speed</i></li><li><b>Mash some vegetables</b><span>Crush a few potato or bean pieces against the pot and stir.</span><i style="--s:4">Speed</i></li><li><b>Beurre mani&eacute;</b><span>Equal parts soft butter and flour, whisked in a little at a time.</span><i style="--s:4">Speed</i></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="sp-s" id="freeze"><div class="sp-w sp-frz"><div><p class="sp-k">Batch planner</p><h2>Cook once, eat three times</h2><p class="sp-lead">Most stews freeze beautifully. Tell us what you are making and we will plan the portions.</p><label for="fz-m">Portions in the pot<input id="fz-m" type="number" min="2" max="40" value="8"></label><label for="fz-e">Eating tonight<input id="fz-e" type="number" min="0" max="20" value="2"></label><label for="fz-c">Portions per container<select id="fz-c"><option value="1">1 (lunches)</option><option value="2" selected>2</option><option value="4">4 (family)</option></select></label></div><div class="sp-fz-o" id="fz-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></section>

<section class="sp-film" aria-label="Photos of stews"><div class="sp-film-in"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792296441582-e5c0f77d7344?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=300&q=75" alt="a woman stirring a large pan of stew at a food stall" width="420" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>A market stew, stirred to order</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792427566393-5c55fb19adb7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=300&q=75" alt="a bowl of green soup with meat, corn on the cob and cilantro" width="420" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Green broth with corn and herbs</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793671313686-078a4dabdf88?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=300&q=75" alt="a plate of braised meat in a dark savoury sauce" width="420" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Braised in a dark, glossy sauce</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792767643741-7a6749a97dbd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=300&q=75" alt="a braised pork knuckle in a dark sauce in a white bowl" width="420" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Pork knuckle, slow and sticky</figcaption></figure></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-dark"><div class="sp-w"><div class="sp-chalk"><p class="sp-k">On the board tonight</p><h2>Two guides from the kitchen</h2><ul><li><a href="one-pot-stew-guide.html"><b>The One-Pot Stew Guide</b><span class="sp-dots"></span><em>Browning, layering, timing</em></a></li><li><a href="freezing-stews-guide.html"><b>Freezing Stews Guide</b><span class="sp-dots"></span><em>Cool, pack, thaw, reheat</em></a></li></ul></div></div></section>

